n\": \"Search for peer-reviewed studies, benchmark reports, and real-world deployments that provide measurable data on the performance of each KV-cache compression method. Specifically collect: (1) memory reduction percentages (e.g., 2x, 4x, 6x), (2) accuracy degradation (e.g., BLEU, perplexity, human evaluation), (3) inference throughput (tokens/sec or requests/sec), (4) latency overhead, and (5) stability under long-context inputs (e.g., 16K+ tokens). Prioritize sources from academic journals, industry whitepapers, and published benchmarks.\",\n      \"step_type\": \"research\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"need_search\": false,\n      \"title\": \"Synthesize and Compare Trade-offs Across Methods\",\n      \"description\": \"Analyze the collected data to identify patterns in the trade-offs between memory savings, accuracy, and throughput across different compression techniques. Compare methods based on their suitability for different use cases (e.g., high-accuracy vs. high-throughput, long-context vs. short-context). Evaluate the reliability and consistency of reported results, and identify potential biases or missing data. Provide a structured comparison table that includes method, memory savings, accuracy impact, throughput impact, and key limitations.\",\n      \"step_type\": \"analysis\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
